From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:56:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] host/companion: Eden Duo's ACNH reader and its guest-memory
 interface

Vendor the Eden Duo ACNH companion module, its ABI headers, the BC decoder, zstd and the data-driven interface manifest into dm/third_party. Only the ACNH profile opts in, through companion.mk; other games link no companion at all. The combined build that includes it is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later, with its notices and the component licenses; the rest of the source tree stays MIT.

The host side reads the guest's own running game through hle_svc.c's locked heap helpers (not a bare vm_read), suspends the guest threads for an expect-guarded inventory write batch, and merges the companion's short A / D-pad presses into player 1's input. It is compiled and linked but not yet activated: the iOS front end that drives DMCompanion is a later step.

Checked: both the ACNH and a non-companion game's dmhost link, the Duo harness (41), test_docs, test_patches and the orientation policy.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: The ACNH companion: Eden Duo's reader and the band a phone standing up shows it in; nxnative carries it on feat/acnh-companion
Issue: none yet: no upstream issue for the companion

